ok   target splits into path and query_string
ok   query_string is empty when absent
ok   header lookup is case-insensitive
ok   header lookup works for headers given in mixed case
ok   content_length parses the header and defaults to 0
ok   content_type keeps only the media type
ok   keep_alive? for HTTP/1.1
ok   keep_alive? for HTTP/1.0
ok   keep_alive? matches Connection tokens exactly, not substrings
ok   content_length of an overlong all-digit value is at least Int64 max
ok   method predicates
ok   override_method! upper-cases the new method
ok   cookie_header returns the Cookie header or empty string
ok   body and headers are exposed
ok   utf8_query_string and utf8_body are the validated text, the same object on every call
ok   utf8_query_string and utf8_body: a raw invalid byte raises QueryMalformed on every call
ok   path_segments decodes once and returns the same Array every time
ok   path_segments: an invalid decoded byte sequence is QueryMalformed and is not cached
ok   path_segments: a raw invalid byte anywhere in the path is QueryMalformed, as is half a character raw
ok   form_value and query_value: the last pair wins, absent is empty
ok   form_value and query_value decode keys and values like a parse
ok   form_value and query_value: name[]= and name[x]= evict an earlier scalar, a later name= writes it again
ok   form_value and query_value: MAX_PAIRS segments are counted, one more is QueryTooMany; invalid bytes are QueryMalformed
ok   form_value on the 4096 x 32 body answers like the parse
ok   content_encoding is the lowercased header, empty when absent
ok   decoded_body is the body itself without a Content-Encoding or with identity
ok   decoded_body inflates a gzip body once and returns the same String every time
